{"cut_proposal":{"candidate_errors":[],"prefix":"To solve the problem, we need to determine the ratio \\( \\frac{PQ}{AQ} \\) where \\( P \\) is the centroid of the regular tetrahedron \\(ABCD\\) and \\(Q\\) is the point where the line \\(AP\\) intersects the face \\(BCD\\).\n\nFirst, let's establish some properties of the regular tetrahedron. The centroid \\(P\\) of a regular tetrahedron divides each median in the ratio 3:1, with the longer segment being from the vertex to the centroid. This means that if we consider the median from vertex \\(A\\) to the centroid of the opposite face \\(BCD\\), the centroid \\(P\\) is located such that \\(AP:PP' = 3:1\\), where \\(P'\\) is the centroid of the face \\(BCD\\).\n\nThe centroid \\(P'\\) of the face \\(BCD\\) is the point where the medians of the equilateral triangle \\(BCD\\) intersect. Since \\(P'\\) is the centroid of the equilateral triangle, it divides each median in the ratio 2:1. Therefore, the distance from \\(P'\\) to any vertex of the triangle (say \\(B\\)) is \\( \\frac{2}{3} \\) of the median length of the triangle.\n\n","prefix_end":996,"status":"review_required"},"eligible":true,"generation":{"generation":{"max_new_tokens":2048,"temperature":0.7,"top_k":0,"top_p":1.0},"ids":[1249,11625,279,3491,11,582,1184,311,8253,279,11341,17767,1124,37018,90,47,48,15170,92073,92,1124,8,1380,17767,393,1124,8,374,279,58119,315,279,5792,27853,32507,291,2248,17767,1867,6484,57758,323,17767,48,57758,374,279,1459,1380,279,1555,17767,2537,57758,88184,279,3579,17767,4897,35,59,3593,5338,11,1077,594,5695,1045,5888,315,279,5792,27853,32507,291,2248,13,576,58119,17767,47,57758,315,264,5792,27853,32507,291,2248,64828,1817,22553,304,279,11341,220,18,25,16,11,448,279,5021,10238,1660,504,279,11936,311,279,58119,13,1096,3363,429,421,582,2908,279,22553,504,11936,17767,32,57758,311,279,58119,315,279,14002,3579,17767,4897,35,59,701,279,58119,17767,47,57758,374,7407,1741,429,17767,2537,25,4406,6,284,220,18,25,16,59,701,1380,17767,47,15777,8